now a forest fire doesn't begin  out of control forest fires might begin  you know when somebody throws a  cigarette out of their car and it slowly  grows and develops into a a pretty big  fire so is fire alive I hope you know  the answer to this question is no of  course not fire is not a living organism  but it does possess some of the  qualities of life well let's look at  something else something that should be  a little more obvious is a car alive  well is a car made of cells parts of it  you could argue yes you know leather  interior and the cloth interior of a car  maybe the wood paneling some cars have  wood on them so you could say that parts  of cars are made from cells does a car  require energy yes of course well a car  responded to its environment what  depends upon the car some cars with  advanced technology will respond to you  know dry and Sun and wetness of the road  can a car reproduce no not at all can a  car grow and develop  well no humans have developed cars and  built them and assembled them so our car  is alive you can see that cars do have  some qualities of life our cars living  of course not  no not at all but I hope you see the  point I'm making with the fire example  in the car example there's a lot of  objects that will possess some of these  qualities of life but in order to be  considered living we think we have a  pretty good checklist here what it means  to be alive so as we wrap up this video  you know if you're in my bio class you  know try to answer these questions and a  separate sheet of paper and I'm happy to  check your answers before school or  after school one day hope you found this  video helpful thanks for watching
 

